{% comment %}
  The Hold still page (holdstill.js): the visitor's own scan. Kept out of
  _pages/hold-still.md so prettier leaves its HTML indented.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hold" data-hold>
  <h1 class="hold-title">Hold still</h1>
  <p class="hold-lead">
    In a scanner you are asked to keep still, and here is why. The scanner measures k‑space, the image's frequencies, one line every half second, and
    every line comes from wherever you are at that moment. Be the patient: your camera stands in for the scanner. The picture stays on this device;
    nothing is recorded or sent.
  </p>
  <div class="piece-art kspace hold-art">
    <figure>
      <canvas data-k role="img" aria-label="Your k-space"></canvas>
      <figcaption>k-space</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <canvas data-img role="img" aria-label="You, rebuilt from the lines measured"></canvas>
      <figcaption data-caption>you</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="kspace-controls">
      <p class="hold-camera"><button type="button" data-camera>use the camera</button></p>
      <p class="kspace-plans" role="group" aria-label="Scan">
        <button type="button" data-plan="full">every line <span data-time></span></button>
        <button type="button" data-plan="fourth">every fourth line <span data-time></span></button>
        <button type="button" data-plan="eighth">every eighth line <span data-time></span></button>
      </p>
      <p class="kspace-status">
        <span data-clock></span>
        <span data-status aria-live="polite">Use the camera to be the patient, or scan the cat.</span>
      </p>
      <p class="kspace-fill" role="group" aria-label="Fill in the missing lines">
        <button type="button" data-coils aria-pressed="false" hidden>unfold with 8 coils</button>
        <button type="button" data-net aria-pressed="false" hidden>coils and a network</button>
        <button type="button" data-save hidden>save the scan</button>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="hold-more"><a href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}">The cat that started it, on the home page&nbsp;→</a></p>
</div>
